{"seq":14,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-08-saltmarsh-summary/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:01:54.926Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"d867188466617a7ae4990ddcc98d347c06e2d5304ca04817cefd36b77147cc02","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Sofia, here are the three answers for your Saltmarsh Provisions summary.\n\n1. **Handover:** Bettina Kroll took the account over from you on Monday, 6 October 2025.\n   - Moss's Coastal note of 5 Oct says Saltmarsh \"changes hands tomorrow, Monday, October 6\". It doesn't name the new owner.\n   - The channel does. On 15 Oct you called it \"Bettina's grocery account\", and on 17 Nov Bettina called it \"Sofia's old grocery account\".\n   - Moss's 2 Nov digest about an ownership change on 3 Nov is about Pellucid Harbor Logistics, not Saltmarsh, so I left it out.\n\n2. **Discount:** 10%.\n   - On 17 Nov 2025 at 14:19, Bettina posted that the discount was 12%.\n   - At 14:24 she corrected it: \"please ignore my earlier note, it's 10%\". She said she had misread June Osei-Lark's draft worksheet.\n   - I've only quoted what was posted here. I haven't checked it against a contract.\n\n3. **Corinne's admin access issue:** ticket **PD-4827**.\n   - Kwame opened it on 15 Oct 2025. The admin option was missing from Corinne's account, and it wasn't a failed sign-in.\n   - Don't confuse it with PD-4824 in Moss's May coverage note. That one is the reefer door-move exception report."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
